        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0546" n="476" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg476"/>

                <head>No. 265.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 19, 1883</date>.
                        (Received December 3.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 666.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I take great pleasure in transmitting
                    herewith a copy of a letter addressed to me by the chairman of the executive
                    committee of the Great International Fisheries Exhibition, London, 1883,
                    requesting me to convey to the Government of the United States the special
                    expression by his royal highness the Prince of Wales, the president, and the
                    members of the executive committee, of their gratitude for the admirable manner
                    in which our Government has so effectively and generously responded to the
                    appeal for co-operation in the past exhibition.</p>
                <p>I am also requested to bring to the notice of the Government of the United States
                    the valuable services of Professor Goode and other gentlemen in organizing the
                    American section of the exhibition and in the jury department.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d265-a1.xml" xpointer="d265-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
